    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** serving as our clear focal point. With a score of 66.98, **Kyle Tucker** is our only \"Strong\" play, benefiting from a favorable 4.07 xERA matchup against Landen Roupp. While we are navigating several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.63) also presents significant upside; he draws a strong platoon advantage against Corbin Burns and benefits from an auxiliary boost due to favorable wind conditions. Conversely, **Heliot Ramos** (42.73) and **Dominic Smith** (41.71) remain near the bottom of our active threshold. Their scores are suppressed by tough opposing arms\u2014specifically Emmet Sheehan and Ben Brown\u2014making them marginal starts that we are keeping in the lineup primarily to avoid burning game caps while awaiting clearer data.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Andy Pages** (57.86), who narrowly missed the \"Strong\" classification. While **Andy Pages** occupies a prime #4 spot in the lineup, his upside is capped slightly by an elite opposing catcher's pop time, which diminishes his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our internal weighting. We have opted to start him to maximize potential RBI production, but he remains the first player we would look to swap if late-breaking weather reports indicate unfavorable conditions. With **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** off today, our offense lacks its usual ceiling, requiring us to be diligent about monitoring the status of **Sam Antonacci** and **Drake Baldwin**. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains our primary concern on the IL, and we continue to monitor the bench availability of **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Nolan Schanuel** to ensure our substitution strategy remains fluid if any last-minute lineup changes occur.",
